WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.534 --> 00:00:03.300
-Our next guest is a very funny
comedian whose new book,

00:00:03.300 --> 00:00:05.767
"A Bathroom Book for People
Not Pooping or Peeing

00:00:05.767 --> 00:00:07.901
But Using the Bathroom
as an Escape,"

00:00:07.901 --> 00:00:09.901
is available November 16th.

00:00:09.901 --> 00:00:12.667
Season three of his show,
"Joe Pera Talks with You,"

00:00:12.667 --> 00:00:14.868
premieres November 7th
on Adult Swim.

00:00:14.868 --> 00:00:16.334
Let's take a look.

00:00:16.334 --> 00:00:20.601
-At what point does it go
from sitting to laying down?

00:00:20.601 --> 00:00:23.601
-45 degrees?
-That makes sense.

00:00:23.601 --> 00:00:26.400
-I always say when you see
more ceiling than wall.

00:00:26.400 --> 00:00:27.701
[ All laugh ]

00:00:27.701 --> 00:00:30.133
[ Laughter ]

00:00:30.133 --> 00:00:33.234
-Please welcome back to
the show our friend Joe Pera.

00:00:33.234 --> 00:00:34.801
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:34.801 --> 00:00:42.000
♪♪

00:00:42.000 --> 00:00:49.200
♪♪

00:00:49.200 --> 00:00:52.267
Welcome back, Joe.
It's so lovely to see you.

00:00:52.267 --> 00:00:56.234
-It's very nice to be here and
have the audience here again.

00:00:56.234 --> 00:00:58.501
-Yeah.
It's so -- Very exciting.

00:00:58.501 --> 00:01:01.434
-We're very excited
to have you, as always.

00:01:01.434 --> 00:01:03.934
Your excitement, as always,
is palpable.

00:01:03.934 --> 00:01:05.501
[ Laughter ]

00:01:05.501 --> 00:01:09.033
In that clip -- I always love,
you know, reminding you of this,

00:01:09.033 --> 00:01:11.901
that you're in that clip
with Gene Kelly...

00:01:11.901 --> 00:01:13.534
-Right.
-...who was a cameraman

00:01:13.534 --> 00:01:14.901
on this show.
-Mm-hmm.

00:01:14.901 --> 00:01:16.734
-You came on this show.
You met him.

00:01:16.734 --> 00:01:19.834
You basically hired him away
from his life as a cameraman

00:01:19.834 --> 00:01:21.300
and he became an actor.

00:01:21.300 --> 00:01:22.801
-I'm sorry.

00:01:22.801 --> 00:01:24.868
[ Laughter ]

00:01:24.868 --> 00:01:26.634
But -- Yeah.

00:01:26.634 --> 00:01:29.834
He retired from this show
last year,

00:01:29.834 --> 00:01:34.100
and then I asked him
to come do one more season

00:01:34.100 --> 00:01:36.834
of the television program,
and he was just --

00:01:36.834 --> 00:01:38.601
I think he just wanted to rest,

00:01:38.601 --> 00:01:40.901
but he's such a nice guy
that he couldn't say no,

00:01:40.901 --> 00:01:44.734
and I'm glad --
-And you did let himself rest

00:01:44.734 --> 00:01:47.501
because that scene was about
picking out a La-Z-Boy for him.

00:01:47.501 --> 00:01:50.200
So, really,
all his acting had to be

00:01:50.200 --> 00:01:51.601
was sitting
in a comfortable chair.

00:01:51.601 --> 00:01:54.901
-Yes, exactly. The episode's
about helping him

00:01:54.901 --> 00:01:57.734
pick out a retirement chair.

00:01:57.734 --> 00:01:59.701
I guess something that's --

00:01:59.701 --> 00:02:04.501
he could sit and unpack
the last 72 years of his life

00:02:04.501 --> 00:02:06.300
while watching daytime TV.

00:02:06.300 --> 00:02:07.567
-Yeah. How was --

00:02:07.567 --> 00:02:09.868
You obviously take a chair
very seriously

00:02:09.868 --> 00:02:11.334
and its level of comfort.

00:02:11.334 --> 00:02:13.901
And since we have you here
and you have a good eye for it,

00:02:13.901 --> 00:02:15.701
how is the chair you're in now?

00:02:15.701 --> 00:02:18.734
-It's, uh -
It's pretty nice, actually.

00:02:18.734 --> 00:02:22.334
It's very exciting to think
of all the celebrities

00:02:22.334 --> 00:02:24.400
who have sat here
over the years

00:02:24.400 --> 00:02:26.133
like Elizabeth Taylor and such.

00:02:26.133 --> 00:02:27.567
-Yeah.

00:02:27.567 --> 00:02:30.434
[ Laughter ]

00:02:30.434 --> 00:02:33.601
Now...

00:02:33.601 --> 00:02:36.033
Joe, you have a very specific
title of this book,

00:02:36.033 --> 00:02:38.501
"A Bathroom Book for People
Not Pooping or Peeing

00:02:38.501 --> 00:02:40.334
But Using the Bathroom
as an Escape."

00:02:40.334 --> 00:02:42.367
Was it important for you
to make sure they knew

00:02:42.367 --> 00:02:45.534
exactly what kind of book
they were buying?

00:02:45.534 --> 00:02:48.434
-The publishing company
said it's way too long,

00:02:48.434 --> 00:02:50.234
but I don't know.

00:02:50.234 --> 00:02:51.968
I see --

00:02:51.968 --> 00:02:54.801
It's very nice when you
have to read it out loud on TV.

00:02:54.801 --> 00:02:56.467
It makes me chuckle backstage.

00:02:56.467 --> 00:02:58.667
[ Laughter ]

00:02:58.667 --> 00:03:04.434
But I just love that things
that kind of are what they say,

00:03:04.434 --> 00:03:06.968
and I wanted to make sure
everybody knows

00:03:06.968 --> 00:03:09.667
what they're getting
as soon as they see the book.

00:03:09.667 --> 00:03:11.334
-You have a few tips in here,

00:03:11.334 --> 00:03:13.434
not just for how to spend
the time in the bathroom

00:03:13.434 --> 00:03:18.133
but, you know, how to re-enter
the social event they were at.

00:03:18.133 --> 00:03:19.634
Sort of like things you can say

00:03:19.634 --> 00:03:22.300
to break the ice
post-trip to the bathroom.

00:03:22.300 --> 00:03:23.601
Could you share a few of those?

00:03:23.601 --> 00:03:24.767
-Sure.
-Yeah.

00:03:24.767 --> 00:03:26.167
-Do you mind?
-Yeah, go for it.

00:03:26.167 --> 00:03:27.801
-Thanks. Yeah.

00:03:27.801 --> 00:03:31.400
Basically, I wanted
to make it easy for people

00:03:31.400 --> 00:03:34.467
to rejoin the party
or whatever else they're doing.

00:03:34.467 --> 00:03:39.601
So I wrote an epilogue
that's all kind of --

00:03:39.601 --> 00:03:40.868
-This is the epilogue.

00:03:40.868 --> 00:03:42.167
-Yes.
-Yeah.

00:03:42.167 --> 00:03:45.467
-And some conversation starters
that you can use

00:03:45.467 --> 00:03:47.334
on the other side of the door.

00:03:47.334 --> 00:03:48.534
[ Laughter ]

00:03:48.534 --> 00:03:52.200
Such as...
you can ask the person,

00:03:52.200 --> 00:03:54.767
"Do you believe
in free will or fate?"

00:03:54.767 --> 00:03:56.868
[ Laughter ]

00:03:56.868 --> 00:03:59.834
"And then depending
on their answer,

00:03:59.834 --> 00:04:01.534
you can drink their drink."

00:04:01.534 --> 00:04:03.467
[ Laughter ]

00:04:12.367 --> 00:04:15.300
"Do Kit-Kats count
as granola bars?"

00:04:15.300 --> 00:04:17.634
[ Laughter ]

00:04:17.634 --> 00:04:20.267
Could talk for hours about that.
-Sure.

00:04:20.267 --> 00:04:24.767
Now, can I ask another question?
You've got the book done.

00:04:24.767 --> 00:04:27.601
Another season of
"Joe Pera Talks to You."

00:04:27.601 --> 00:04:31.000
When you have these works
behind you in your rear-view,

00:04:31.000 --> 00:04:33.667
do you start focusing
on things, other projects

00:04:33.667 --> 00:04:35.367
that you want to get done?
-Yeah.

00:04:35.367 --> 00:04:39.767
I'm kind of in that nice period
right now where we're able to,

00:04:39.767 --> 00:04:43.100
you know,
feel free of the ideas,

00:04:43.100 --> 00:04:45.767
feel like we did a good-enough
job and can put them down,

00:04:45.767 --> 00:04:49.234
and now I've been thinking
about new ones to pick up.

00:04:49.234 --> 00:04:51.334
And I actually found this pitch.

00:04:51.334 --> 00:04:55.167
This a real pitch
that I pitched to Adult Swim.

00:04:55.167 --> 00:04:56.300
-Okay.

00:04:56.300 --> 00:04:57.834
-At the same time
as the original

00:04:57.834 --> 00:05:00.334
"Joe Pera Talks You to Sleep."

00:05:00.334 --> 00:05:03.234
-Uh-huh.
-And they chose that one.

00:05:03.234 --> 00:05:04.434
-But this is the other one?

00:05:04.434 --> 00:05:05.934
-This is the other one
that could have been.

00:05:05.934 --> 00:05:08.067
And I wanted to share it
with you in case,

00:05:08.067 --> 00:05:10.200
I don't know, you're interested
in producing it.

00:05:10.200 --> 00:05:12.367
-Okay.

00:05:12.367 --> 00:05:14.434
Do you want me to read
about it a little bit?

00:05:14.434 --> 00:05:16.133
-Sure.
-Or do you want me to --

00:05:16.133 --> 00:05:17.701
It's called "My Two Cars."

00:05:17.701 --> 00:05:19.734
[ Laughter ]

00:05:19.734 --> 00:05:23.434
-It's a real pitch I wrote
with my buddy Dan Licata.

00:05:23.434 --> 00:05:24.868
-Yeah, a very funny man.

00:05:24.868 --> 00:05:27.767
-Uh-huh. And you want to read
the tag line at the top?

00:05:27.767 --> 00:05:29.200
-Sure. "'My Two Cars.'

00:05:29.200 --> 00:05:32.100
With great cars
comes great responsibility."

00:05:32.100 --> 00:05:33.901
-Right.
-Okay.

00:05:33.901 --> 00:05:36.934
-And then the summary is

00:05:36.934 --> 00:05:39.968
"Imagine -- you're lucky enough

00:05:39.968 --> 00:05:44.801
to own both a PT Cruiser
and a Mini Cooper.

00:05:44.801 --> 00:05:46.901
[ Laughter ]

00:05:46.901 --> 00:05:49.934
Your day-to-day life
would be insane."

00:05:49.934 --> 00:05:51.334
[ Laughter ]

00:05:55.634 --> 00:05:57.200
"Keith Ass [bleep]

00:05:57.200 --> 00:06:01.367
does own both of these
exciting cars.

00:06:01.367 --> 00:06:04.033
And while things
are really, really good,

00:06:04.033 --> 00:06:06.067
there's one problem.

00:06:06.067 --> 00:06:09.067
You can only drive
one car at a time."

00:06:09.067 --> 00:06:10.534
[ Laughter ]

00:06:10.534 --> 00:06:14.834
But no matter which car Keith
chooses, it's always a trip."

00:06:14.834 --> 00:06:16.267
And then...
-Can you just read --

00:06:16.267 --> 00:06:18.334
Can I read?
-Yeah, please.

00:06:18.334 --> 00:06:20.067
-This is -- Episode three
would be the one

00:06:20.067 --> 00:06:21.934
that would sell me.
-Yes.

00:06:21.934 --> 00:06:24.167
-This is where I would
green-light it.

00:06:24.167 --> 00:06:25.767
"Keith goes to
the premiere of a film

00:06:25.767 --> 00:06:29.367
by P.T. Anderson
starring Bradley Cooper.

00:06:29.367 --> 00:06:30.901
When he shows up
in his PT Cruiser,

00:06:30.901 --> 00:06:32.267
P.T. Anderson loves it.

00:06:32.267 --> 00:06:34.968
Unfortunately,
Bradley Cooper hates it.

00:06:34.968 --> 00:06:38.434
So Keith takes the subway home

00:06:38.434 --> 00:06:41.567
and drives back
in his Mini Cooper

00:06:41.567 --> 00:06:43.300
to prove he has both."

00:06:43.300 --> 00:06:44.934
That is...

00:06:44.934 --> 00:06:46.534
[ Applause ]

00:06:46.534 --> 00:06:47.868
...gold.

00:06:47.868 --> 00:06:49.534
-Thank you.

00:06:49.534 --> 00:06:53.133
Dan Licata asked me
to include one thing

00:06:53.133 --> 00:06:55.801
that we left out --
that Keith Ass [bleep]

00:06:55.801 --> 00:06:57.667
is also Supreme Court justice.

00:06:57.667 --> 00:07:00.200
[ Laughter ]

00:07:00.200 --> 00:07:03.033
So it's gives it a little depth
and, you know...

00:07:03.033 --> 00:07:05.267
-Yeah. Sure. I felt like there
wasn't enough going on with

00:07:05.267 --> 00:07:06.968
Keith Ass [bleep].

00:07:06.968 --> 00:07:09.501
That's Joe Pera, everybody.

00:07:09.501 --> 00:07:11.734
"A Bathroom Book for People
Not Pooping or Peeing

00:07:11.734 --> 00:07:13.467
But Using the Bathroom
as an Escape"

00:07:13.467 --> 00:07:14.701
is available November 16th.

00:07:14.701 --> 00:07:16.767
And season three of
"Joe Pera Talks with You"

00:07:16.767 --> 00:07:19.133
premieres November 7th
on Adult Swim.

